Correct": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a69b"}, {"id": "ee1afc", "text": "AND", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a69c"}, {"id": "839b3e", "text": "OR", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a69d"}, {"id": "24fa47", "text": "NAND", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a69e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a69f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e39"], "question": {"text": "Refer to the circuit diagram given in the figure. which of the following observations are correct?\nA. Total resistance of circuit is $6 \\Omega$\nB. Current in Ammeter is 1 A\nC. Potential across $A B$ is 4 Volts.\nD. Potential across CD is 4 Volts\nE. Total resistance of the circuit is $8 \\Omega$.\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FB_NrMfkxxosqTaVE7_gmT0JGEy5nZC3XdzT1S9fucsY.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "e75072", "text": "A, B and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a0"}, {"id": "07f837", "text": "A, B and C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a1"}, {"id": "70616d", "text": "A, C and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a2"}, {"id": "23a5aa", "text": "B, C and E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa392"], "question": {"text": "To get output <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#39;1&#39;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> at <math><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> for the given logic gate circuit the input values must be:</mi><br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F659934b7-0a09-4733-bb37-7ead5cd383bb-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 366px; height: 160px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "9b857e", "text": "<math><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a5"}, {"id": "19c8d8", "text": "<math><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a6"}, {"id": "e44c5a", "text": "<math><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a7"}, {"id": "cb1a4c", "text": "<math><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6a9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "Choose the correct statement about Zener diode:"}, "options": [{"id": "d44b97", "text": "It works as a voltage regulator in reverse bias and behaves like simple p-n junction diode in forward bias", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6aa"}, {"id": "8a9ebf", "text": "It works as a voltage regulator in both forward and reverse bias", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6ab"}, {"id": "932269", "text": "It works a voltage regulator only in forward bias", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6ac"}, {"id": "73f5ba", "text": "It works as a voltage regulator in forward bias and behaves like simple p-n junction diode in reverse bias", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6ad"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a6ae", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4