imumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:20.197Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:20.197Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a753"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a74f", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a72b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "<p>In a given circuit diagram, a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> zener diode along with a series resistance is connected across a&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;power supply. The minimum value of the resistance required, if the maximum zener current is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math> will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#937;.</mtext></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb91cb447-5427-4cd7-851a-3be7e131d972-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 433px; height: 192px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d64e07", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a72c"}, {"id": "3059cf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a72d"}, {"id": "0bfbbd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a72e"}, {"id": "8ccd39", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a72f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a730", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the circuit shown below, maximum Zener diode current will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8442604a-603c-487b-8d83-64ed57722a78-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 126px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a8ad60", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a731"}, {"id": "acfb1f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a732"}, {"id": "e1fb73", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a733"}, {"id": "df87ba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a734"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a735", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "<p>A zener diode of power rating <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> is to be used as a voltage regulator. If the zener diode has a breakdown of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and it has to regulate voltage fluctuated between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math> for safe operation should be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8433487d-7b09-455a-a663-d2fd4ae913eb-16de8932-8de0-400a-8197-5cbe63710257-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 138px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "8510e5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a736"}, {"id": "594ca9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a737"}, {"id": "fe507b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a738"}, {"id": "b5e5dc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a739"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a73a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "<p>A Zener of breakdown voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and maximum Zener current, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>ZM</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math> is subjected to an input voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> with series resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. In the given circuit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub></math> represents the variable load resistance. The ratio of maximum and minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math> is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe4e916d1-1489-4802-9b5b-fbb0a93297a8-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 170px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f2ff5d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a73b"}, {"id": "0fb98f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a73c"}, {"id": "325a16", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a73d"}, {"id": "9a5fe5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a73e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a73f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "<p>A zener diode having zener voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi></math> and power dissipation rating of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>W</mi></math> is connected across a potential divider arranged with maximum potential drop across zener diode is as shown in the diagram. The value of protective resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></math> is&nbsp;_____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa152405f-d08f-40c7-b1da-6433f0171521-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 235px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b7f7ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a740"}, {"id": "350d1c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a741"}, {"id": "221d14", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925a742"}, {"id": "c16f30", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "